gamutant.css's Okhsl and Okhsv parts (.gamut-okhsl, .gamut-okhsl-from, .gamut-okhsv) follow ok_color.h's maths and constants
(https://bottosson.github.io/misc/ok_color.h), and for Display P3 the constants in Isaac Muse's okhsl_p3.py (2023, linked
from csswg-drafts #8659: ok_color.h adapted to Python and adjusted to Display P3, under Ottosson's notice). The adaptive
method of .gamut-fit-screen and .gamut-fit-gradient (--gamut-method: adaptive) is gamut_clip_adaptive_L0_L_cusp from
Ottosson's gamut clipping code (https://bottosson.github.io/posts/gamutclipping/, alpha 0.05), ported to CSS. The checks'
references test/ref/okhsl.mjs, test/ref/ottosson.mjs and test/vendor/okhsl-fit.mjs port the same code to JavaScript, and
test/data/okhsl-p3-coloraide.json holds ColorAide's outputs with Isaac Muse's constants (https://github.com/facelessuser/coloraide,
MIT; ColorAide itself is not redistributed). All
