Sample code from two W3C drafts, under the W3C Software and Document License (2023), below:
- .gamut-color-extract and .gamut-okhsl-from carry CSS Color 4's conversion matrices (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-4/).
- .gamut-rec2100-pq, .gamut-rec2100-hlg, .gamut-rec2100-linear, .gamut-jzazbz, .gamut-jzczhz and .gamut-ictcp follow CSS
  Color HDR's decoding (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-hdr-1/), changed: its Jzazbz decode's matrix products put in
  order, ninv defined, the division by 203 restored, and its ICtCp decode returning relative XYZ.
